      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's not about 'stopping' in a dramatic sense; it's about choosing an exit strategy when the fight is purely self-destructive. Courage isn't always about enduring the fire; sometimes it's about recognizing that the fire is consuming *you*, and choosing to step out of the heat. That quiet departure is often the most honest act of self-preservation when everything else has become unbearable.",
      "source": "target",
